== the CLASS dimension: what order does the body use? ==
loop.py:283  mask = mask_of(k for k in obs.kinds if 0 <= k <= 15)
loop.py:297  kind = kind_of(EMIT(mask));  loop.py:298  mask = ADVANCE(mask)
EMIT is m & -m -> lowest set bit -> classes are tried in ASCENDING KIND-ID
order. Kind id is the number the dictionary registered the class under. It
is not evidence, and rank.py never sees it: the ranking law ranks LINES.

winning class's position among the classes on its own line (body order): {'1/1': 11, '1/2': 3, '2/2': 3, '2/3': 5, '3/3': 1, '3/4': 3, '4/4': 1}
winner was the FIRST class tried on its line in 14/27 fixtures; NOT first in 13

